# Esc puts the transient toasts away (Rust clears its toast stack on every
# Esc). Two pickers that have nothing to show each leave a toast; one Esc
# clears both. They used to stack until their TTL ran out (walkthrough 1.11).
command picker.recent
expect screen contains "no recent files"
command picker.clipboard
expect screen contains "no registers hold anything yet"
expect screen contains "no recent files"
key esc
expect screen lacks "no recent files"
expect screen lacks "no registers hold anything yet"
